# What this repository tracks, and what it does not.
#
# The instance files in data/ and the raw per-run records in results/ ARE tracked, on purpose.
# They are the input and the evidence behind every table, figure and quoted number in the
# article, so nothing below excludes either directory.
#
# Everything listed here is regenerated by building or by running the experiments.

# ---- build output -------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
compile_commands.json
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# ---- Python bytecode ----------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---- generated by the analysis ------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloned on its own, analyse.py finds no main.tex above it and writes these inside the
# repository rather than beside the paper.  They are derived from results/ and are rebuilt by
#   python3 scripts/analyse.py
tables/
figures/

# A --quick run is a reduced smoke test; it writes its records here so that it cannot overwrite
# the full design the article was built from.
results-quick/

# ---- expanded instance files --------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ ships gzipped and scripts/run_all.sh expands each file beside its archive on first run,
# keeping the .gz.  The .gz are tracked; the expansions (and the copies that
# `experiments instances --data data` rewrites) are not.
data/*.txt
!data/*.txt.gz

# ---- editor and OS noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
